# compile-census: per-file `bin/bend --check-only` over the 102 .bend that checks/substrate.py's POP_ROOT=tinybendygrad/ does not walk.
# taken=2026-10-22T17:18:36Z  committed=97  untracked=5  ::  A SNAPSHOT. `discover()` walks the WORKING COPY, so that count is `len(discover())` AT THIS MOMENT and it MOVES as drivers land; a run whose `handed=` differs from the number on the line above is the tree having moved, not this file being wrong. Re-run to re-take it.
# state= WARM|COLD|NO-MEASUREMENT|NO-INSTRUMENT|<state>?NOTOKEN  token= checks/bounded.py's OWN verdict token, read off stderr because its exit status cannot mean one thing.
# first_line= the instrument's first stderr line, or the verdict row.
# cause= the COMPILER's OWN error shape, from `checks/substrate.py`'s `CAUSES` table
#   (loaded by path) applied LINE BY LINE -- `substrate.cause_of()` searches the whole
#   output and its `^`-anchored patterns never match, because a bend failure's first
#   line is `SOME PROOFS FAIL` and the error is on the second.  `COLD` ALONE IS A
#   NOISE: every failure in the tree shares the sentence `SOME PROOFS FAIL`, and a
#   FRAGMENT and a driver whose constructor was deleted upstream must not be read
#   the same way.
# sha= the file's sha256, so the record is keyed on CONTENT.  `checks/differ.py`'s
#   `substrate_digest()` says why: "Never on st_mtime".  A reader can now tell a
#   census that describes THIS tree from one that describes last week's.
# error= the compiler's OWN line, verbatim, so a row names the error and not a
#   class of it.  This is the column `gates/compile-census-gate.py` prints.
# **THE COLUMN NAMES ARE IN THIS HEADER AND NOT IN A LINE OF THEIR OWN, AND THAT IS
# A FIX AND NOT A STYLE.** MEASURED 2026-10-20 on `gates/edge-runner.py`'s reader of
# a generated `.rows`: with the column line written as DATA, the reader parsed it as
# a row whose key was the literal string `gate`, and the edge's plan then reported
# `STALE gate` -- a gate that does not exist, named by the file's own vocabulary.
# The house style agrees: `gates/crp_graph_census-pins.rows` puts its column names
# in the `#` header and writes no column line at all.
# ceiling 2048 MB, 300 s, ONE bend process at a time.
# columns: state, peak_MB, token, file, cause, sha, error, first_line
